# Dev Notes 48 — Runtime Capability Bus Executor Skeleton v1

**Date:** 2026-06-18  
**Branch:** `runtime-capability-bus-executor-skeleton-v1`  
**Status:** **Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared contract/skeleton-only scope; assistant sandbox syntax checks, targeted executor-skeleton smoke, existing contract-chain smokes, fixture helper check, worker import-cycle check, public-entrypoint guard, artifact guard, package extraction/recheck, Michael-run local Windows/MINGW64 candidate checks, direct GitHub branch inspection, and direct GitHub `main` inspection passed. No real-runtime test is required for the declared contract/skeleton-only scope because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds a narrow executor skeleton handoff seam after the existing Capability Bus execute-action descriptor chain.

The descriptor chain is now:

```text
actionEnvelope
  -> capability bus action
  -> router route plan
  -> service plan
  -> backend adapter plan
  -> capability execution plan
  -> executor skeleton handoff descriptor
```

The new executor skeleton descriptor is metadata-only. It makes the future executor handoff boundary explicit without executing services, invoking backend adapters, calling the runtime, calling the worker bridge, or touching worker behavior.

---

## 2. Scope

Added:

```text
runtime/execution/capabilityExecutorSkeletonCommon.mjs
runtime/execution/capabilityExecutorSkeletonPlan.mjs
tests/smokeTestCapabilityBusExecutorSkeleton.mjs
docs/dev-notes.48
```

Modified:

```text
runtime/execution/capabilityExecutorContract.mjs
tests/smokeTestCapabilityExecutorContract.mjs
README.md
docs/README.md
docs/current-architecture.md
```

No bus execute-action behavior was changed. The execute-action plan remains accepted at the existing execution-plan layer; the executor skeleton lives under `runtime/execution/` as a future handoff descriptor seam.

---

## 3. New contract identity

```text
contractVersion: capability-executor-skeleton.v1
status: planned
```

Boundary metadata:

```js
{
    executor: "skeleton-only",
    executable: false,
    adapterInvocation: "not-implemented",
    runtimeWiring: "not-wired"
}
```

The descriptor embeds a validated capability execution plan and copies the normalized invocation metadata:

```text
actionId
runId
capability
serviceId
adapterId
backendKind
routeId
modelBundleId
hardwareProfileId
stream
timeoutMs
resultContract
eventContract
```

---

## 4. Contract behavior

The executor skeleton plan helpers:

```js
validateCapabilityExecutorSkeletonPlan(value)
normalizeCapabilityExecutorSkeletonPlan(value)
assertCapabilityExecutorSkeletonPlan(value)
```

Behavior:

```text
accepts a current capability execution plan or an existing skeleton descriptor;
validates the embedded execution plan through the current capability execution plan validator;
copies invocation metadata from the execution plan;
requires the boundary block to remain skeleton-only and non-executable;
rejects unknown top-level, invocation, and boundary fields;
rejects forbidden executable/raw backend/model-path keys;
rejects mismatched invocation metadata;
returns copy-isolated normalized descriptors.
```

---

## 5. Architecture boundaries preserved

This branch does not:

```text
change runtime.mjs public APIs
add executeAction() public API
implement executeAction() behavior
call capability services
invoke backend adapters
call workerBridge
import llama_worker
load models
enqueue runtime requests
stream tokens
change scheduler/request/stream behavior
change cancellation or timeout behavior
change lifecycle/init/reset/shutdown behavior
expand configOverride
add request-time raw model paths or projector paths
implement memory/storage behavior
implement Cognitive Graph Runtime behavior
implement multimodal/vision execution
```

The executor skeleton remains a contract-only handoff descriptor for a later behavior-wiring branch.

